{
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  // mof-crux-aurora-codex: real cross-HPC MOF pipeline running entirely on
// a Codex ChatGPT subscription (no Argo). Model: gpt-5.6-luna via
// openai-codex SDK, ChatGPT Plus / Team / etc.
  //
  // Crux planner_executor  (chemgraph.multi_agent, CPU)
  //   mofforge_build -> run_ase[UMA opt] -> pacmof2_assign_charges
  //   -> transfer_file (eagle -> flare) -> send_message(aurora_sim)
  //   -> wait for reply -> finish_turn.
  //
  // Aurora aurora_sim      (chemgraph.single_agent, XPU/SYCL)
  //   wait_for_message -> run_graspa_ensemble -> transfer_file
  //   (flare -> eagle) -> send_message(planner_executor) -> finish_turn.
  //
  // Endpoint UUIDs:
  //   CRUX/EAGLE:  05d2c76a-e867-4f67-aa57-76edeb0beda0  (alcf#dtn_eagle)
  //   AURORA/FLARE: f39a7a0f-5bfc-46ce-9615-ba9f8592814f  (alcf#dtn_flare)
  //
  // Aurora env vars (set in submit_defaults or the PBS wrapper):
  //   CHEMGRAPH_GRASPA_BIN=/flare/ChemGraph/jinchu/gRASPA/graspa-sycl/bin/sycl.out
  //
  // Prereqs (one-time):
  //   1. mkdir /flare/ChemGraph/jinchu/inbox-aurora on aurora login.
  //   2. mkdir /eagle/ChemGraph/jinchu/inbox-crux on crux login.
  //   3. gRASPA-sycl binary at $CHEMGRAPH_GRASPA_BIN.
  //   4. ChemGraph dev editable-installed in academy-dev venvs on both.
  //   5. fairchem-core + pacmof2 installed via pip --no-deps in venvs.
  //
  // MCP servers: library, not per-site inventory
  // --------------------------------------------
  // The `mcp_servers` block below is a shared library of MCP server
  // definitions. There is no per-site list. Each site's daemon reads
  // the whole library, then only spawns the subset the running agent
  // whitelists via `agent.mcp_servers` (see daemon.py:72-77 --
  // `[spec for spec in campaign.mcp_servers if spec.name in
  // agent_spec.mcp_servers]`). Nothing idles: an MCP that isn't in
  // the running agent's whitelist is never started on that site.
  //
  // Site -> MCP for this campaign:
  //   Crux    (planner_executor) -> mofforge, chemgraph, pacmof2, globus
  //   Aurora  (aurora_sim)       -> graspa, globus
  //
  // The site->MCP mapping is implicit through which agent runs where,
  // set by the launcher's --agents slice (federated spawn-site flow).
  //
  // $VIRTUAL_ENV in each command is expanded at spawn time from the
  // daemon's own sys.executable (mcp_supervisor.py), so one shared
  // library entry resolves to /eagle/.../academy-dev/bin/python on
  // Crux and /flare/.../academy-dev/bin/python on Aurora without
  // editing the JSON per site.
  //
  // Kickoff (recipient = planner_executor):
  //   {"spec":{"topology":"pcu","backend":"pormake",
  //     "node_files":["<pormake bbs dir>/N59.xyz"],
  //     "edge_files":["<pormake bbs dir>/E32.xyz"],
  //     "output_dir":"/lus/eagle/projects/ChemGraph/jinchu/mof-out/build"},
  //    "opt_output_json":"/lus/eagle/projects/ChemGraph/jinchu/mof-out/opt.json",
  //    "charges_output_dir":"/lus/eagle/projects/ChemGraph/jinchu/mof-out/charges",
  //    "adsorbate":"H2O","temperature_k":298.15,"pressure_pa":101325.0}
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  "run_id": "mof-crux-aurora-codex",
  "user_task": "Build a MOF on Crux, optimize + charge it, hand off to Aurora for gRASPA GCMC uptake, report result.",
  "prompt_profile": "prompt_profiles/default.json",
  "initial_agent": "planner_executor",
  "launch_defaults": {
    "lm_config_template": "codex-gpt5.6-luna",
    "agent_count": 2,
    "agents_per_node": 1,
    "max_decisions": 24
  },
  "resources": {},
  "mcp_servers": [
    {
      "name": "mofforge",
      "command": "$VIRTUAL_ENV/bin/python -m mofforge.mcp.server"
    },
    {
      "name": "chemgraph",
      "command": "$VIRTUAL_ENV/bin/python -m chemgraph.mcp.mcp_tools"
    },
    {
      "name": "pacmof2",
      // Real PACMOF2 (thin wrapper around the pip package, single-CIF).
      "command": "$VIRTUAL_ENV/bin/python -m chemgraph.academy.tools.pacmof2_mcp"
    },
    {
      "name": "globus",
      "command": "$VIRTUAL_ENV/bin/python -m chemgraph.academy.tools.globus_flex_mcp"
    },
    {
      "name": "graspa",
      // Real gRASPA MCP (dev branch). Aurora venv Python path.
      // Ensemble-shaped: takes a directory + conditions, fans out one
      // job per (structure, condition). For a single MOF pass a
      // singleton list under input_structures.
      "command": "$VIRTUAL_ENV/bin/python -m chemgraph.mcp.graspa_mcp_hpc"
    }
  ],
  "agents": [
    {
      "name": "planner_executor",
      "role": "MOFPlannerExecutor",
      "mission": "Do EXACTLY these steps in order, one tool call each. Never repeat a step. Copy paths and args from the inject message verbatim; do NOT invent paths. Every step uses the previous step's output as input.\n\nStep 1: mofforge_build with ALL of these args from the inject: topology, backend, node_files, edge_files, output_dir. The 'backend' arg is REQUIRED and MUST be exactly the value from the inject (e.g. 'pormake'). Response gives output_paths[0] -- call this BUILT_CIF.\n\nStep 2: run_ase with params={input_structure_file: BUILT_CIF, output_results_file: <opt_output_json from inject>, driver: 'opt', optimizer: 'fire', fmax: 0.05, steps: 200, calculator: {calculator_type: 'FAIRChem', model_name: 'uma-s-1p1', task_name: 'omat', device: 'cpu'}}. The 'task_name' and 'model_name' are REQUIRED. Response confirms opt done -- the OPT_CIF is BUILT_CIF (opt writes back in place).\n\nStep 3: pacmof2_assign_charges with cif_path=OPT_CIF and output_dir=<charges_output_dir from inject>. Response gives charges_cif -- call this CHARGED_CIF.\n\nStep 4: transfer_file with source_endpoint='05d2c76a-e867-4f67-aa57-76edeb0beda0', source_path=CHARGED_CIF, dest_endpoint='f39a7a0f-5bfc-46ce-9615-ba9f8592814f', dest_path='/ChemGraph/jinchu/inbox-aurora/' + basename(CHARGED_CIF), wait=true. Response confirms upload.\n\nStep 5: send_message(recipient='aurora_sim', content=JSON with dest_path, adsorbate, temperature_k, pressure_pa from inject, reply_requested=true).\n\nStep 6: wait for aurora_sim's reply, then finish_turn with a one-line summary including the reported uptake numbers.",
      "allowed_peers": ["aurora_sim"],
      "mcp_servers": ["mofforge", "chemgraph", "pacmof2", "globus"],
      "allowed_tools": [
        "mofforge_build",
        "run_ase",
        "pacmof2_assign_charges",
        "transfer_file",
        "check_transfer_status",
        "list_files"
      ],
      "behavior_graph": {
        "entry": "decide",
        "nodes": {
          "decide": {
            "type": "llm_decide",
            "params": {"engine": "chemgraph.multi_agent"},
            "next": "decide"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "aurora_sim",
      "role": "GRASPASimulator",
      "mission": "You are the adsorption-simulation specialist on Aurora (XPU/SYCL). You receive messages from planner_executor with a CIF path (already staged on YOUR endpoint) and adsorbate conditions (temperature K, pressure Pa, adsorbate name). Your job:\n\n(1) run_graspa_ensemble with params={input_structures: [<cif path from message>], adsorbate: <from message>, conditions: [{temperature: <from message>, pressure: <from message>}], n_cycles: 10000, output_result_file: 'raspa.log'}. This is an ensemble tool; pass the single CIF as a one-element list. Response is a list of per-(structure,condition) result dicts; the single element has the uptake numbers plus an output path.\n\n(2) transfer_file the result file back to Crux. source_endpoint='f39a7a0f-5bfc-46ce-9615-ba9f8592814f' (Aurora/flare), source_path=<result output path>, dest_endpoint='05d2c76a-e867-4f67-aa57-76edeb0beda0' (Crux/eagle), dest_path='/ChemGraph/jinchu/inbox-crux/' + basename(<result output path>), wait=true.\n\n(3) send_message(recipient='planner_executor', reply_requested=false) with a JSON containing the uptake numbers and the remote result path.\n\n(4) finish_turn. Do NOT initiate contact -- respond to messages only.",
      "allowed_peers": ["planner_executor"],
      "mcp_servers": ["graspa", "globus"],
      "allowed_tools": [
        "run_graspa_ensemble",
        "transfer_file",
        "check_transfer_status",
        "list_files"
      ],
      "behavior_graph": {
        "entry": "decide",
        "nodes": {
          "decide": {
            "type": "llm_decide",
            "params": {"engine": "chemgraph.single_agent"},
            "next": "decide"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
